            <ArticleTitle>Exacerbation of angina pectoris by prazosin.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1213-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of angina pectoris worsened by prazosin is presented. Since a hypertensive population includes many patients with known or occult coronary artery disease, physicians should use prazosin cautiously in this subgroup, particularly when beta-adrenergic antagonists cannot be used concurrently.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
